{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"383","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Vowels"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Iahubina is tired of so many complicated languages, so she decided to invent a new, simple language. She already made a dictionary consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" 3-words. A 3-word is a sequence of exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" lowercase letters of the first 24 letters of the English alphabet ("},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"a"},{"kind":"text","text":" to "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"x"},{"kind":"text","text":"). She decided that some of the letters are vowels, and all the others are consonants. The whole language is based on a simple rule: any word that contains at least one vowel is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"correct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Iahubina forgot which letters are the vowels, and wants to find some possible correct sets of vowels. She asks Iahub questions. In each question, she will give Iahub a set of letters considered vowels (in this question). For each question she wants to know how many words of the dictionary are correct, considering the given set of vowels."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Iahubina wants to know the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xor"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the squared answers to all the possible questions. There are "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"224"},{"kind":"text","text":" different questions, they are all subsets of the set of the first 24 letters of the English alphabet. Help Iahub find that number."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer, "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 104)"},{"kind":"text","text":". Each of the next "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" lines contains a 3-word consisting of "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"3"},{"kind":"text","text":" lowercase letters. There will be no two identical 3-words."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one number, the "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"xor"},{"kind":"text","text":" of the squared answers to the queries."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5\nabc\naaa\nada\nbcd\ndef\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"383E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/383/problem/E"}